### What rule do you want to change?

no-shadow

### What change do you want to make?

Generate more warnings

### How do you think the change should be implemented?

A new default behavior

### Example code

[playground](https://eslint.org/play/#)

```js
function wrap(y) {
  return () => {
    console.log('wrapped');
    y();
  };
}
let x = false;
export const a = wrap(function a() {
  if (!x) {
    x = true;
    a();
  }
});
```

### What does the rule currently do for this code?

no errors

### What will the rule do after it's changed?

error on `a` - the function declaration is shadowing the const and importantly they are not equal to the same thing.

E.g. if I have

```
const a = function a() {}
```

I think it is ok to not give a no-shadow error.

but when it is:

```
const a = wrap(function a() {})
```

a !== a

